# Caddy terminates TLS for the RAW endpoint.
#
# HTTPS is not optional: the site is served over HTTPS, and a browser refuses
# to call an HTTP endpoint from an HTTPS page (mixed content). So the Oracle
# box needs a real domain with an A record pointing straight at its IP.
#
# Point the A record DIRECTLY at the Oracle IP. Do NOT enable Cloudflare's
# orange-cloud proxy on this record: proxying it would serve the RAW endpoint
# from Cloudflare's Dhaka PoP and the RAW number would silently become a
# second BDIX number.

raw.example.com {
	encode off
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080 {
		flush_interval -1
	}
}
